       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 2400 mg four times daily comes to 9,600 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day, and the OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day. A single 2400 mg dose is also three times the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level there is a serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and CNS and metabolic toxicity.\n\nYou may have meant 2400 mg per day in total. These are the common ways to write that:\n- 600 mg PO four times daily (2400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2400 mg/day)\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, ideally after checking with your resident or attending. I'll enter the order once you confirm. Also tell me the indication, such as pain or inflammatory arthritis, if you want it added to the order note."
